@startuml flow-transaction
title Flow of WATCH / MULTI / EXEC (with an optimistic-lock abort)

actor "Client A" as A
actor "Client B" as B
participant "Dispatcher\n(shared)" as CD
participant "Session A\n(per connection)" as SA
participant Store

== WATCH ==
A -> CD : WATCH foo
CD -> SA : watch("foo")
SA -> Store : versionOf("foo")  => 7
SA -> SA : watchedVersions = {foo: 7}
CD --> A : +OK

== MULTI ==
A -> CD : MULTI
CD -> SA : beginMulti()   // inMulti = true
CD --> A : +OK

A -> CD : INCR foo
note right of CD : inMulti && not EXEC/DISCARD/WATCH
CD -> SA : queue(["INCR","foo"])
CD --> A : +QUEUED

== another client mutates the watched key ==
B -> CD : SET foo 99
CD -> Store : set("foo","99")
Store -> Store : touch("foo")  // keyVersions[foo] = 8

== EXEC ==
A -> CD : EXEC
CD -> SA : inMulti()? yes
CD -> SA : endMulti()
CD -> SA : isAnyWatchedKeyDirty()
SA -> Store : versionOf("foo")  => 8
SA -> SA : 8 != snapshot 7  => DIRTY
SA --> CD : true
CD -> SA : clearQueue(); clearWatches()
CD --> A : *-1\\r\\n   (nil — transaction aborted)

note over CD, Store
If NOT dirty: drainQueue(), then for each queued
command call dispatch(cmd, session) recursively,
concatenating replies into  *<n>\\r\\n ...
end note

@enduml